WEBVTT

00:15:26.044 --> 00:15:30.763
So I think we were helping inform culture.

00:15:30.787 --> 00:15:34.723
I think companies were looking to us

00:15:34.747 --> 00:15:38.114
to think about culture in a different way.

00:15:38.958 --> 00:15:40.663
I would say the unfortunate part

00:15:40.687 --> 00:15:44.909
is I think they gave too much emphasis
to the space itself.

00:15:44.933 --> 00:15:46.293
And that, you know,

00:15:46.317 --> 00:15:48.560
what one of my colleagues
at WeWork at the time

00:15:48.584 --> 00:15:50.040
called cultural confetti,

00:15:50.064 --> 00:15:52.611
and much more of the appliqué of culture

00:15:52.635 --> 00:15:57.635
than, like, the deep internals of culture.

00:15:58.387 --> 00:16:00.869
So I think we were trying
to have those conversations